      "text": "The 6-portfolio file contains the 2x3 size and prior-return (2\u201312 month) value-weighted intersections. Ken French's UMD is the average of the two High-momentum portfolios minus the average of the two Low-momentum portfolios, so I compute UMD = 0.5\u00b7(Small Hi + Big Hi) \u2212 0.5\u00b7(Small Lo + Big Lo).\n\nThe script reads only the first (value-weighted monthly) block, stopping at the first non-data line so the equal-weighted block and footer are ignored. Missing codes (-99.99 and -999) become NaN, and months lacking any of the four required portfolios are dropped.\n\n```python\nimport re\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nIN_FILE = \"6_Portfolios_ME_Prior_12_2.csv\"\nOUT_FILE = \"output.csv\"\n\n\ndef is_missing(x):\n    return np.isclose(x, -99.99, atol=1e-6) or np.isclose(x, -999.0, atol=1e-6)\n\n\ndef parse_first_monthly_block(path):\n    \"\"\"Parse the first contiguous block of YYYYMM rows (value-weighted monthly returns).\"\"\"\n    rows = []\n    started = False\n    date_re = re.compile(r'^\\s*(\\d{6})\\s*,(.*)$')\n    with open(path, encoding=\"latin-1\") as f:\n        for line in f:\n            s = line.strip().lstrip(\"\\ufeff\")\n            m = date_re.match(s)\n            if m:\n                started = True\n                ym = int(m.group(1))\n                month = ym % 100\n                if not (1 <= month <= 12):\n                    continue\n                parts = [p.strip() for p in m.group(2).split(\",\")]\n                vals = []\n                for p in parts[:6]:\n                    try:\n                        v = float(p)\n                    except ValueError:\n                        v = np.nan\n                    if not np.isnan(v) and is_missing(v):\n                        v = np.nan\n                    vals.append(v)\n                while len(vals) < 6:\n                    vals.append(np.nan)\n                rows.append([ym] + vals)\n            elif started:\n                # end of the first monthly block (footer / next block)\n                break\n    cols = [\"date\", \"SL\", \"SM\", \"SH\", \"BL\", \"BM\", \"BH\"]\n    df = pd.DataFrame(rows, columns=cols)\n    return df\n\n\ndef main():\n    df = parse_first_monthly_block(IN_FILE)\n    df = df.drop_duplicates(subset=\"date\").sort_values(\"date\").reset_index(drop=True)\n\n    needed = [\"SL\", \"SH\", \"BL\", \"BH\"]\n    df = df.dropna(subset=needed).copy()\n\n    # Ken French UMD: average of Small-High and Big-High minus average of Small-Low and Big-Low\n    df[\"value\"] = 0.5 * (df[\"SH\"] + df[\"BH\"]) - 0.5 * (df[\"SL\"] + df[\"BL\"])\n\n    out = df[[\"date\", \"value\"]].copy()\n    out[\"date\"] = out[\"date\"].astype(int)\n    out.to_csv(OUT_FILE, index=False, columns=[\"date\", \"value\"])\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
